{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "class Number:\n    \"\"\"A class to encapsulate an integer value and its reversal logic.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self.value = value\n\n    def reverse(self):\n        \"\"\"Returns the integer value with its decimal digits reversed.\"\"\"\n        return int(str(self.value)[::-1])\n\n    def isOneLessThanTwiceReverse(self):\n        \"\"\"Checks if the stored number is one less than twice its reverse.\"\"\"\n        reversed_val = self.reverse()\n        return self.value == (2 * reversed_val) - 1\n\ndef check(n):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given number is one less than twice its reverse.\"\"\"\n    number_instance = Number(n)\n    return number_instance.isOneLessThanTwiceReverse()"}
