{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m), which counts permutations of {1, ..., n} with m ascents.\n    It uses a dynamic programming approach based on the recurrence relation.\n    \"\"\"\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case for the recurrence\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table using the recurrence relation:\n    # A(i, j) = (j+1) * A(i-1, j) + (i-j) * A(i-1, j-1)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i):  # j goes from 0 to i-1\n            term1 = (j + 1) * dp[i - 1][j]\n            term2 = 0\n            if j - 1 >= 0:\n                term2 = (i - j) * dp[i - 1][j - 1]\n            dp[i][j] = term1 + term2\n\n    return dp[n][m]"}
