{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def _proper_divisor_sum(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a given number.\"\"\"\n    if num <= 1:\n        return 0\n    s = 1\n    for i in range(2, int(num**0.5) + 1):\n        if num % i == 0:\n            s += i\n            if i * i != num:\n                s += num // i\n    return s\n\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sums all amicable numbers from 1 up to a specified number n.\"\"\"\n    divisor_sums = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        divisor_sums[i] = _proper_divisor_sum(i)\n\n    amicable_set = set()\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        s = divisor_sums[i]\n        if s > i and s <= n and divisor_sums[s] == i:\n            amicable_set.add(i)\n            amicable_set.add(s)\n\n    return sum(amicable_set)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum difference between the number of 0s and 1s in any substring.\n    Uses a Kadane's-style algorithm for maximum and minimum subarray sums.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not binary_string:\n        return 0\n\n    # Transform the binary string: '0' becomes 1, '1' becomes -1.\n    # A subarray sum then represents (count of 0s) - (count of 1s).\n    transformed_arr = []\n    for char in binary_string:\n        if char == '0':\n            transformed_arr.append(1)\n        else:  # char == '1'\n            transformed_arr.append(-1)\n\n    # Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum subarray sum (max_zeros_minus_ones)\n    max_so_far = float('-inf')\n    current_max = 0\n    for x in transformed_arr:\n        current_max += x\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n\n    # Kadane's algorithm to find the minimum subarray sum (min_zeros_minus_ones)\n    # This is a symmetric version of Kadane's where we reset if current sum becomes positive.\n    min_so_far = float('inf')\n    current_min = 0\n    for x in transformed_arr:\n        current_min += x\n        min_so_far = min(min_so_far, current_min)\n        if current_min > 0:\n            current_min = 0\n            \n    # The maximum difference is the larger of the absolute values of:\n    # 1. The maximum (0s - 1s) difference found (max_so_far).\n    # 2. The maximum (1s - 0s) difference found, which is -min_so_far (absolute value of the most negative 0s - 1s difference).\n    return max(abs(max_so_far), abs(min_so_far))"}
