{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def sum(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of common positive divisors of two integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _get_divisors(n):\n        \"\"\"Helper to find all positive divisors of a number.\"\"\"\n        divs = set()\n        if n == 0:\n            return divs\n        n = abs(n)\n        i = 1\n        while i * i <= n:\n            if n % i == 0:\n                divs.add(i)\n                divs.add(n // i)\n            i += 1\n        return divs\n\n    divisors_a = _get_divisors(a)\n    divisors_b = _get_divisors(b)\n\n    common_divs = divisors_a.intersection(divisors_b)\n\n    # Manually sum the common divisors to avoid conflict with the function name 'sum'.\n    total_sum = 0\n    for d in common_divs:\n        total_sum += d\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/129", "solution": "def magic_square_test(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates whether the given square matrix is a magic square.\n    A magic square is a square matrix where the sum of each row, each column,\n    and both main diagonals is the same.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(matrix)\n\n    # FR3: Validate Square Matrix - Check if the matrix is square and not empty\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n    \n    for row in matrix:\n        if len(row) != n:\n            return False\n\n    # FR4: Compute Sums - Calculate the target sum (sum of the first row)\n    target_sum = sum(matrix[0])\n\n    # Check row sums\n    for row in matrix:\n        if sum(row) != target_sum:\n            return False\n\n    # Check column sums\n    for j in range(n):\n        col_sum = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            col_sum += matrix[i][j]\n        if col_sum != target_sum:\n            return False\n\n    # Check main diagonal sum\n    main_diag_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        main_diag_sum += matrix[i][i]\n    if main_diag_sum != target_sum:\n        return False\n\n    # Check anti-diagonal sum\n    anti_diag_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        anti_diag_sum += matrix[i][n - 1 - i]\n    if anti_diag_sum != target_sum:\n        return False\n\n    # FR5: Return Boolean Result - If all checks pass, it's a magic square\n    return True"}
