{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-positioned bits of a given number to 1 while preserving odd bits.\n    Even positions are interpreted as 1-indexed from the right (e.g., positions 2, 4, 6,...),\n    which correspond to 0-indexed bit positions 1, 3, 5,...\n    \"\"\"\n    if value == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Determine the bit-width of the input number.\n    # For positive numbers, this is the position of the highest set bit + 1.\n    bit_width = value.bit_length()\n\n    # Construct a mask where 0-indexed odd bits are set to 1.\n    # The design document refers to \"even positions (bit positions 2,4,6,...)\"\n    # which correspond to 0-indexed odd bits (1,3,5,...).\n    # The mask string '10' creates a pattern of ...101010 when interpreted as binary.\n    # The length of the mask string is adjusted to cover at least bit_width.\n    mask_length_factor = (bit_width + 1) // 2\n    raw_mask_str = '10' * mask_length_factor\n    mask = int(raw_mask_str, 2)\n\n    # Apply the mask using bitwise OR to set the specified bits.\n    result = value | mask\n\n    # Ensure the result fits within the original bit-width by masking out higher bits.\n    # This prevents the number from growing unnecessarily in bit length if the mask\n    # extended beyond the original highest set bit of 'value'.\n    final_width_mask = (1 << bit_width) - 1\n    return result & final_width_mask"}
