{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers strictly less than n.\n    Uses an optimized prime checking helper function.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_prime(num):\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if a number is prime using a 6k +/- 1 optimization.\n        \"\"\"\n        if num <= 1:\n            return False\n        if num <= 3:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(2, n):\n        if _is_prime(i):\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "from typing import Tuple\n\ndef maximize_elements(tuple1: Tuple[Tuple[int, ...], ...], tuple2: Tuple[Tuple[int, ...], ...]) -> Tuple[Tuple[int, ...], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the element-wise maximum of two tuples of tuples.\n\n    Raises ValueError if the input tuples have different shapes.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same number of sub-tuples.\")\n\n    result_sub_tuples = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        sub_t1 = tuple1[i]\n        sub_t2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        if len(sub_t1) != len(sub_t2):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Sub-tuples at index {i} have different lengths: {len(sub_t1)} vs {len(sub_t2)}.\")\n\n        result_elements = []\n        for j in range(len(sub_t1)):\n            result_elements.append(max(sub_t1[j], sub_t2[j]))\n        result_sub_tuples.append(tuple(result_elements))\n\n    return tuple(result_sub_tuples)"}
