{"task_id": "Mbpp/282", "solution": "from typing import List, Union\n\nNumber = Union[int, float]\n\ndef _validate_lengths(list1: List[Number], list2: List[Number]) -> None:\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists must have the same length.\")\n\ndef _validate_numeric(elements: List[Number]) -> None:\n    if not all(isinstance(x, (int, float)) for x in elements):\n        raise TypeError(\"All elements must be numeric.\")\n\ndef sub_list(list1: List[Number], list2: List[Number]) -> List[Number]:\n    \"\"\"Subtract two lists element-wise, returning a new list of differences.\n    Raises ValueError if lengths differ, TypeError if non-numeric elements are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_lengths(list1, list2)\n    _validate_numeric(list1)\n    _validate_numeric(list2)\n    return [a - b for a, b in zip(list1, list2)]"}
