{"task_id": "Mbpp/290", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef max_length(list_of_lists: List[List[int]]) -> Tuple[int, List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the list of maximum length in a list of lists.\n    Returns a tuple containing the maximum length and the first sub-list that achieves this length.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_len = 0\n    result_list: List[int] = []\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        current_len = len(sublist)\n        if current_len > max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n            result_list = sublist\n\n    return (max_len, result_list)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/285", "solution": "def text_match_two_three(text):\n    # Checks if the string contains 'a' followed by two or three 'b' characters.\n    # It performs a linear scan through the input string to find the pattern.\n    n = len(text)\n    for i in range(n):\n        if text[i] == 'a':\n            # Check for 'abb' pattern\n            if i + 2 < n and text[i+1] == 'b' and text[i+2] == 'b':\n                # If 'abb' is found, check if it extends to 'abbb'\n                if i + 3 < n and text[i+3] == 'b':\n                    return True  # Pattern 'abbb' found\n                else:\n                    return True  # Pattern 'abb' found (not 'abbb')\n    return False"}
