{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "def first_non_repeating_character(input_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first non-repeated character in a given string.\n    Returns None if no non-repeating character is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    char_counts = {}\n    char_order = []\n\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char not in char_counts:\n            char_counts[char] = 0\n            char_order.append(char)\n        char_counts[char] += 1\n\n    for char in char_order:\n        if char_counts[char] == 1:\n            return char\n\n    return None"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "from typing import List\n\nclass SumOfDigitsFunction:\n    \"\"\"Helper class to encapsulate the logic for summing digits.\"\"\"\n\n    def compute(self, numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the sum of digits for each number in the list.\"\"\"\n        total_sum_of_all_digits = 0\n        for number in numbers:\n            # Use absolute value to correctly sum digits for negative numbers.\n            # Convert to string to iterate through digits easily.\n            for digit_char in str(abs(number)):\n                total_sum_of_all_digits += int(digit_char)\n        return total_sum_of_all_digits\n\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of digits of each number of a given list, delegating\n    the core logic to a helper class.\n    \"\"\"\n    calculator = SumOfDigitsFunction()\n    return calculator.compute(numbers)"}
