{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of integers using the Shell sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Start with a large gap, then reduce the gap\n    gap = n // 2\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            # Add arr[i] to the elements that have been gap sorted\n            # Save arr[i] in temp and make a hole at position i\n            temp = arr[i]\n            # shift earlier gap-sorted elements up until the correct\n            # location for arr[i] is found\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            # put temp (the original arr[i]) in its correct location\n            arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/429", "solution": "from typing import Tuple\n\ndef and_tuples(tuple1: Tuple[int], tuple2: Tuple[int]) -> Tuple[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the element-wise bitwise AND of two input tuples.\n    Raises ValueError if tuples are not of equal length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length\")\n\n    return tuple(a & b for a, b in zip(tuple1, tuple2))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/432", "solution": "def median_trapezium(a: float, b: float, c: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the median length of a trapezium as the average of its two parallel sides.\n    Raises TypeError if inputs are not numeric.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not all(isinstance(x, (int, float)) for x in (a, b, c)):\n        raise TypeError(\"All inputs must be numeric values.\")\n    return (a + b) / 2.0"}
