{"task_id": "Mbpp/430", "solution": "def parabola_directrix(a: float, b: float, c: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the y-coordinate of the directrix for a parabola y = ax^2 + bx + c.\n    This function validates inputs and calculates the directrix based on the standard formula.\n    \"\"\"\n    for name, value in ((\"a\", a), (\"b\", b), (\"c\", c)):\n        if not isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Parameter '{name}' must be numeric, got {type(value).__name__}\")\n\n    if a == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Coefficient 'a' must be non-zero for a valid parabola.\")\n\n    directrix = c - (b ** 2 + 1) / (4 * a)\n    return float(directrix)"}
