{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "def index_multiplication(tuple1: tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...], tuple2: tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...]) -> tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs index-wise multiplication of elements in two tuples of tuples.\n    Raises ValueError if input tuple lengths or inner tuple lengths mismatch.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    if not tuple1:\n        return ()\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        inner_t1 = tuple1[i]\n        inner_t2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        if len(inner_t1) != len(inner_t2):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Inner tuples at index {i} must have the same length.\")\n\n        inner_result = []\n        for j in range(len(inner_t1)):\n            inner_result.append(inner_t1[j] * inner_t2[j])\n        result.append(tuple(inner_result))\n    \n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/446", "solution": "from typing import Any, List, Tuple\n\ndef count_Occurrence(data: Tuple[Any, ...], elements: List[Any]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return total occurrences of any element from `elements` in `data`.\"\"\"\n    if not data or not elements:\n        return 0\n    element_set = set(elements)\n    return sum(1 for item in data if item in element_set)"}
