{"task_id": "Mbpp/450", "solution": "import collections\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass StringExtractor:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encapsulates the logic for extracting strings based on their length.\n    \"\"\"\n    def extractString(self, strings: List[str], size: int) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Filters a list of strings, returning only those with a specified length.\n        \"\"\"\n        result = []\n        for s in strings:\n            if len(s) == size:\n                result.append(s)\n        return result\n\ndef extract_string(strings: List[str], size: int) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts specified size of strings from a given list of string values.\n    \"\"\"\n    extractor = StringExtractor()\n    return extractor.extractString(strings, size)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from index 0 to n.\n    Perrin sequence: P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2, P(k)=P(k-2)+P(k-3) for k>2.\n    \"\"\"\n    p0 = 3\n    p1 = 0\n    p2 = 2\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return p0\n    if n == 1:\n        return p0 + p1\n    if n == 2:\n        return p0 + p1 + p2\n\n    current_sum = p0 + p1 + p2\n\n    # p_prev3 holds P(i-3), p_prev2 holds P(i-2), p_prev1 holds P(i-1)\n    p_prev3 = p0\n    p_prev2 = p1\n    p_prev1 = p2\n\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        p_current = p_prev3 + p_prev2\n        current_sum += p_current\n\n        p_prev3 = p_prev2\n        p_prev2 = p_prev1\n        p_prev1 = p_current\n        \n    return current_sum"}
