{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "def armstrong_number(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given integer is an Armstrong number.\n    Returns False for negative input as per definition for Armstrong numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n\n    num_str = str(number)\n    num_digits = len(num_str)\n    armstrong_sum = 0\n\n    for digit_char in num_str:\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        armstrong_sum += digit ** num_digits\n\n    return armstrong_sum == number"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef find_kth(array1: List[int], array2: List[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the k-th smallest element from the union of two sorted arrays.\n    Raises IndexError if k is out of bounds.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 1 or k > len(array1) + len(array2):\n        raise IndexError(\"k is out of bounds\")\n\n    # Ensure we always binary search on the smaller array\n    if len(array1) > len(array2):\n        array1, array2 = array2, array1\n\n    m, n = len(array1), len(array2)\n    low, high = 0, m\n\n    while low <= high:\n        partition_a = (low + high) // 2\n        partition_b = k - partition_a\n\n        max_left_a = float('-inf') if partition_a == 0 else array1[partition_a - 1]\n        min_right_a = float('inf') if partition_a == m else array1[partition_a]\n\n        max_left_b = float('-inf') if partition_b == 0 else array2[partition_b - 1]\n        min_right_b = float('inf') if partition_b == n else array2[partition_b]\n\n        if max_left_a <= min_right_b and max_left_b <= min_right_a:\n            return max(max_left_a, max_left_b)\n        elif max_left_a > min_right_b:\n            high = partition_a - 1\n        else:\n            low = partition_a + 1\n\n    raise RuntimeError(\"Failed to find kth element\")"}
