{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "import math\n\ndef get_ludic(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a sorted list of all lucid numbers less than or equal to n.\n    Lucid numbers are defined as 1 and prime numbers for this context.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_prime(k: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if a number is considered \"prime\" in the lucid number context,\n        which includes 1 and actual prime numbers.\n        \"\"\"\n        if k == 1:\n            return True\n        if k < 2:\n            return False\n        if k == 2:\n            return True\n        if k % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        for i in range(3, math.isqrt(k) + 1, 2):\n            if k % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n\n    lucid_numbers = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if _is_prime(i):\n            lucid_numbers.append(i)\n\n    return lucid_numbers"}
