{"task_id": "Mbpp/611", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef max_of_nth(matrix: List[List[int]], column_index: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the maximum value in the specified column of a matrix.\n    Raises ValueError for empty matrix, unequal row lengths, or out-of-bounds column index.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not matrix:\n        raise ValueError(\"Matrix is empty.\")\n\n    num_columns = len(matrix[0])\n\n    for row in matrix:\n        if len(row) != num_columns:\n            raise ValueError(\"All rows must have the same number of columns.\")\n\n    if column_index < 0 or column_index >= num_columns:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Column index {column_index} out of bounds for matrix with {num_columns} columns.\")\n\n    max_value = matrix[0][column_index]\n    for row in matrix[1:]:\n        value = row[column_index]\n        if value > max_value:\n            max_value = value\n\n    return max_value"}
