{"task_id": "Mbpp/723", "solution": "from typing import List, Any\n\ndef count_same_pair(list1: List[Any], list2: List[Any]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Count the number of indices where two equal\u2011length lists have identical values.\n    Raises ValueError if the input lists are of different lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists must have the same length.\")\n\n    count = 0\n    for a, b in zip(list1, list2):\n        if a == b:\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
