{"task_id": "Mbpp/725", "solution": "def _is_escaped(s: str, index: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the character at 'index' is preceded by an odd number of backslashes.\"\"\"\n    if index == 0:\n        return False\n    backslashes = 0\n    i = index - 1\n    while i >= 0 and s[i] == '\\\\':\n        backslashes += 1\n        i -= 1\n    return backslashes % 2 == 1\n\ndef extract_quotation(s: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Extracts values enclosed in non-escaped double quotation marks from a string.\"\"\"\n    result = []\n    n = len(s)\n    i = 0\n    while i < n:\n        if s[i] == '\"' and not _is_escaped(s, i):\n            # Found a starting non-escaped double quote\n            start_content_index = i + 1\n            j = start_content_index\n            while j < n:\n                if s[j] == '\"' and not _is_escaped(s, j):\n                    # Found an ending non-escaped double quote\n                    result.append(s[start_content_index:j])\n                    i = j + 1 # Advance outer loop index past the found quote\n                    break # Break from inner loop, continue search from new i\n                j += 1\n            else:\n                # If inner loop completes without finding a closing quote,\n                # the current opening quote is unclosed. Move past it.\n                i += 1\n                continue # Skip the i+=1 below and start next outer loop iteration\n        # Move to the next character if current one is not a starting quote\n        # or if it's an escaped quote\n        i += 1\n    return result"}
