{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "```python\ndef find_min_diff(values: tuple[int, ...], count: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum difference between any two elements in a given array.\n    Assumes valid input conforming to the design.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_values = sorted(values)\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    for i in range(1, count):\n        diff = sorted_values[i] - sorted_values[i-1]\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n            if min_diff == 0:  # Optimization: if duplicates exist, 0 is the min diff\n                return 0\n    return min_diff\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "def find_nth_polite_number(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth polite number. A polite number is a positive integer that is not a power of two.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_power_of_two(val):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a positive integer is a power of two using a bitwise operation.\"\"\"\n        return val > 0 and (val & (val - 1) == 0)\n\n    polite_count = 0\n    num = 1\n    while True:\n        if not _is_power_of_two(num):\n            polite_count += 1\n            if polite_count == n:\n                return num\n        num += 1"}
