{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(arr, target):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Assumes the input array 'arr' is already sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return -1\n\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            result = mid  # Found a potential last position, try to find one further right\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else: # arr[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1\n            \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Validates inputs to ensure l and r are positive integers and l <= r.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (isinstance(l, int) and isinstance(r, int)):\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs l and r must be integers.\")\n    if l <= 0 or r <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs l and r must be positive integers.\")\n    if l > r:\n        raise ValueError(\"Lower bound l must be less than or equal to upper bound r.\")\n\n    # Determine the first odd number in the range\n    first_odd = l if l % 2 == 1 else l + 1\n\n    # Determine the last odd number in the range\n    last_odd = r if r % 2 == 1 else r - 1\n\n    # If the adjusted first_odd is greater than last_odd, there are no odd numbers in the range\n    if first_odd > last_odd:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate the number of odd terms using arithmetic series properties\n    # The common difference is 2\n    count = (last_odd - first_odd) // 2 + 1\n\n    # Calculate the sum using the arithmetic series sum formula: n * (a1 + an) / 2\n    total_sum = count * (first_odd + last_odd) // 2\n\n    return total_sum"}
