{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit unsigned number left by d bits.\n\n    Validates input number to be within 0 and 0xFFFFFFFF, otherwise raises ValueError.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (0 <= number <= 0xFFFFFFFF):\n        raise ValueError(\"Number must be a 32-bit unsigned integer (0 to 0xFFFFFFFF).\")\n\n    d = d % 32\n    # Perform the left rotation\n    # Shift the bits left by d, and OR them with the bits that wrapped around from the left\n    rotated_number = ((number << d) | (number >> (32 - d)))\n    # Mask the result to ensure it remains within 32 bits\n    return rotated_number & 0xFFFFFFFF"}
